{"orgCode":"3980","name":"Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment","agencyCode":"3890","agencyName":"Environmental Protection","description":"The Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment protects and enhances the health of Californians and the state's environment through scientific evaluations that inform, support, and guide regulatory decisions and other actions. The Office performs risk assessments for various regulatory programs under the California Environmental Protection Agency, as well as other state and local agencies, and provides these programs with scientific tools and information upon which to base risk-management decisions. Distinct programs focus on assessing hazards and health risks, including risks to children and other sensitive subpopulations, from exposure to chemicals in air, drinking water, including microplastics in drinking water, food, pesticides, consumer products, and fish and shellfish, as well as health and environmental impacts from climate change. The Office also evaluates community pollution burdens and vulnerabilities that guide the state's efforts to invest in disadvantaged communities and reduce exposures and risks to residents, and maintains a state-wide extreme heat scoring system designed to raise public awareness of the impacts of extreme heat and to connect communities to locally relevant resources to keep them safe.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":25408,"cy":28580,"by":28805},"positions":{"py":134.3,"cy":148.4,"by":148.4},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":3171,"cy":4124,"by":4109}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/3890/3980","kind":"department","name":"Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment","code":"3980","amounts":{"py":25408,"cy":28580,"by":28805},"positions":{"py":134.3,"cy":148.4,"by":148.4},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":10162,"cy":10992,"by":10822},"special":{"py":15246,"cy":17588,"by":17983}},"children":[{"id":"exp/3890/3980/3730","kind":"program","name":"Health Risk Assessment","code":"3730","amounts":{"py":25408,"cy":28580,"by":28805},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":10162,"cy":10992,"by":10822},"special":{"py":15246,"cy":17588,"by":17983}},"positions":{"py":134.3,"cy":148.4,"by":148.4},"description":"3730 - HEALTH RISK ASSESSMENT\n\nThe Health Risk Assessment program conducts scientific assessments of health and environmental risks of chemicals that enter the environment from many different sources. The program: identifies chemicals with the potential to cause adverse health effects; quantifies risks and recommends health-based goals and standards; develops scientific policies and guidelines for hazard identification and risk assessment; and provides medical, scientific, and public health support, consultation, and training to state regulators, local governmental agencies, and the public. The program pays particular attention to protecting the health of infants and children and other sensitive populations. The program also evaluates community pollution burdens and vulnerabilities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":28579,"cy":32704,"by":32914}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/3890/3980/3730/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":10162,"cy":10992,"by":10822},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":10162,"cy":10992,"by":10822}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":10162,"cy":10992,"by":10822}}}},{"id":"exp/3890/3980/3730/f0028","kind":"fund","name":"Unified Program Account","code":"0028","amounts":{"py":219,"cy":227,"by":227},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":219,"cy":227,"by":227}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":219,"cy":227,"by":227}}}},{"id":"exp/3890/3980/3730/f0044","kind":"fund","name":"Motor Vehicle Account, State Transportation Fund","code":"0044","amounts":{"py":4302,"cy":5147,"by":5164},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":4302,"cy":5147,"by":5164}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":